SetRadioGroupCheckedAction only suppressed OnCheckedChangeListener
on direct children of RadioGroup before calling RadioGroup.check().
However, RadioGroup.check() uses findViewById() recursively across
the entire subtree to set checked states. This allowed a nested
RadioButton in a custom RemoteViews layout to retain its listener,
which fired during reapply and triggered startPendingIntent with
MODE_BACKGROUND_ACTIVITY_START_ALLOW_ALWAYS.

This change replaces direct-child listener suppression with a
recursive subtree walk to ensure all CompoundButton listeners in the
RadioGroup hierarchy are suppressed before check() is called.
